.TH SHARK 1 "2026-07-30" "Shark 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shark \- convert almost any file and download video from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shark convert
.I file ...
.B \-\-to
.I format
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B shark c
.I file ...
.B \-\-to
.I format
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B shark download
.I url ...
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B shark formats
.RI [ category ]
.br
.B shark sources
.RI [ filter ]
.br
.B shark info
.I file
.br
.B shark man
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B shark
is the terminal face of the Shark macOS app. It is not a separate build: the
binary inspects its own invocation name and the first argument, then either
opens the window or stays in the terminal. Conversions performed here and in
the window therefore cannot drift apart \(em the code is the same.
.PP
Four engines sit behind one queue and the right one is chosen automatically
from the pair of input and output formats. Media goes through
.BR ffmpeg ,
images through ImageIO, documents through PDFKit and CoreText, and downloads
through
.BR yt\-dlp .
All of them are bundled inside the application, so nothing has to be installed
separately.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B convert\fR, \fBc
Convert one or more files. Requires
.BR \-\-to .
.B c
is an alias, identical in every respect.
.TP
.B download
Download video or audio from a URL.
.TP
.B formats \fR[\fIcategory\fR]
List the output formats. The optional argument narrows the list to one
category.
.TP
.B sources \fR[\fIfilter\fR]
List the download sources known to the bundled yt\-dlp \(em 1752 extractors at
the time of writing. The count is printed to standard error so that standard
output stays a clean list.
.TP
.B info \fIfile\fR
Print type, size and, for media, duration, resolution and codecs.
.TP
.B man
Open this manual page from inside the application bundle, without installing
it into the system manual path.
.TP
.B help\fR, \fBversion
Print usage or the version.
.SH CONVERT OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-t ", " \-\-to " format"
Target format. Required. See
.B shark formats
for the list.
.TP
.BI \-o ", " \-\-out " directory"
Where results go. Defaults to the directory of each source file.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " name"
Name of the result without extension. Only valid with a single input file.
.TP
.BI \-\-quality " preset"
.BR high ", " balanced " or " compact .
Maps to a CRF preset; affects size far more than it affects perceived quality.
.TP
.BI \-\-resolution " height"
.BR original ", " 2160 ", " 1440 ", " 1080 ", " 720 ", " 480 " or " 360 .
Only ever scales down; a smaller source is left alone.
.TP
.BI \-\-bitrate " kbps"
Audio bitrate:
.BR 96 ", " 128 ", " 192 ", " 256 " or " 320 .
Ignored for lossless targets.
.TP
.BI \-\-image\-quality " 0-100"
Quality for lossy image formats such as jpg, heic and webp.
.TP
.B \-\-strip\-metadata
Drop metadata from the result.
.TP
.B \-\-overwrite
Replace an existing file instead of creating a numbered copy.
.SH DOWNLOAD OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o ", " \-\-out " directory"
Where downloads go. Defaults to ~/Downloads.
.TP
.BI \-\-audio " format"
Audio only:
.BR mp3 ", " m4a ", " opus ", " flac " or " wav .
.TP
.BI \-\-quality " height"
.BR best ", " 2160 ", " 1440 ", " 1080 ", " 720 " or " 480 .
.TP
.BI \-\-container " type"
.BR mp4 ", " mkv " or " webm .
.TP
.BI \-\-cookies " source"
.BR safari ", " chrome ", " firefox ", " edge ,
or a path to a cookies.txt file. Needed for private, age\-restricted and
account\-only videos.
.IP
Safari cookies live in a protected container and require Full Disk Access.
Firefox needs no permission at all, and a cookies.txt file avoids the question
entirely.
.TP
.B \-\-subs
Write and embed ru/en subtitles.
.TP
.B \-\-playlist
Download the whole playlist instead of a single item.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-thumbnail
Do not embed cover art.
.SH OUTPUT
Result paths are written to standard output, one per line. Progress is written
to standard error, and the progress bar is drawn only when standard error is a
terminal. Redirecting standard output therefore yields a clean list of paths
suitable for further processing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Everything succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
At least one file or download failed.
.TP
.B 2
Bad arguments. Unknown options are rejected rather than silently ignored, so a
typo in a flag is an error rather than a quiet change in behaviour.
.TP
.B 3
A required engine is missing from the bundle.
.SH EXAMPLES
Convert a video, leaving the result next to the original:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
shark c clip.mov \-\-to mp4
.EE
.RE
.PP
Convert a folder of camera photographs, writing elsewhere:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
shark c ~/Photos/*.heic \-\-to jpg \-\-image\-quality 90 \-\-out ~/Desktop
.EE
.RE
.PP
Extract audio from a lecture recording:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
shark c lecture.mp4 \-\-to mp3 \-\-bitrate 320
.EE
.RE
.PP
Shrink a large video for sharing:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
shark c big.mov \-\-to mp4 \-\-quality compact \-\-resolution 1080
.EE
.RE
.PP
Turn a document into a PDF under a different name:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
shark c report.docx \-\-to pdf \-\-name "July report"
.EE
.RE
.PP
Collect the resulting paths for a later step:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
shark c *.wav \-\-to mp3 > converted.txt
.EE
.RE
.PP
Walk a tree, which the window cannot do:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
find ~/Video \-name "*.avi" \-exec shark c {} \-\-to mp4 \\;
.EE
.RE
.PP
Download a video, then the same video as audio:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
shark download <url> \-\-quality 1080
shark download <url> \-\-audio mp3 \-\-cookies firefox
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /Applications/Shark.app/Contents/Helpers/shark
The executable, a link to the application binary.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/Shark/Tools/
Updated engines. Looked up before the bundled ones, so an update overrides the
baseline shipped inside the application.
.SH NOTES
Download only what you have the right to: your own uploads, freely licensed
material, or content the rights holder permits you to download. The terms of
each platform are your responsibility.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR yt\-dlp (1)
.PP
Project page: https://github.com/shineexxx/shark
